  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 殿\ntitle: palace; lord\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 13\nradical: 殳\nradicalNumber: 79\nonyomi: [デン, テン]\nkunyomi: [との, -どの]\ndistractors: [段, 投, 役]\n---\n\n# 殿 — palace; lord\n\n**Strokes:** 13 · **Key (radical):** 殳 (no. 79) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n殿 occurs in palace words such as 宮殿 きゅうでん and 御殿 ごてん. 殿 との is also a respectful word for a feudal lord. The bound form -どの has a separate use as a written address suffix.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice the crowded left side beside 殳 and imagine an elaborate palace with a ceremonial object at its side. This is a modern-shape mnemonic, not a historical or phonetic analysis.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| デン | on | 宮殿 きゅうでん - palace |\n| テン | on | [御殿](../words/御殿.md) ごてん - palace |\n| との | kun | 殿 との - feudal lord (respectful) |\n| -どの | kun | 仮殿 かりどの - temporary shrine; word-final どの |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [御殿](../words/御殿.md) ごてん - palace\n- 宮殿 きゅうでん - palace\n- 殿 との - feudal lord\n\n## Notes\n\n- 仮殿 かりどの houses a shrine's sacred object while the main shrine is being repaired. This gives a lexical example of word-final どの in the building sense.\n- Separately, the polite address suffix 殿 -どの attaches to a name or title: for example 部長殿 ぶちょうどの, To the department head, in a written address. JMdict identifies official/business letters and letters to inferiors; it is not a universal upgrade in respect over 様 さま.\n- The palace or mansion sense of 殿 との is marked archaic in JMdict. That qualification does not make the separate modern word 御殿 ごてん archaic.\n- 御殿 ごてん and 宮殿 きゅうでん illustrate different on readings. Learn the whole words instead of choosing デン or テン from the English gloss alone.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1187920, 1228470, 1270560, 1442490, 1442500.\n",
